{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>At the mouth of HaShem the children of Israel would journey, etc.</b> And the cloud would make known what the mouth of HaShem would ordain." "<b>All the days of, etc., and when it prolonged, etc.</b> The verse comes to set forth all the modes of the cloud's guidance, and to teach the praise of Israel — that they were desirous of whatever HaShem desired. And it began with the matter of the prolongation of the encampment's duration and said <b>all the days that the cloud dwelt, they encamped</b> — meaning, יַחֲנוּ: they desired to encamp. Therefore it did not say חָנוּ בְּנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל, which would have given the impression that they did so out of compulsion from the One who leads them. And it further said <b>and when it prolonged</b> etc., to say that even if it prolonged so much, many days, nevertheless they encamped. And its saying <b>and they observed</b> etc. is to say that besides the fact that they encamped all the while, etc., it further informs us that they did not do the thing because they desired sitting and not journeying, but rather because of observance of the word of HaShem — and that is its saying <b>and they observed</b> etc., even though they are many days. And its saying <b>and they would not journey</b> rather than 'and they did not journey' is to exclude the implication as though it said 'and they did not desire to journey.'"], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:07:05.047792592Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}